      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-19T07:59:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This means you can call register multiple times but the 2nd call and further are ignored.\n\n    registerStateCallback(executor1, cb);\n    registerStateCallback(executor2, cb);\n    unregisterStateCallback(cb);\n    unregisterStateCallback(cb);\n\nIf you do this, executor2 is ignored (probably unintended) and the second call to unregister does nothing (because of l.198~199)\n\nIt might be nicer to your callers to either refcount or to reject registering the same callback multiple times (it\u0027s fine if it was unregistered in the mean time).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 181,
        "startChar": 42,
